00:03:39.763 --> 00:03:41.810
- And for, one more time, for the people

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.150
that are learning about
you, real quick, on,

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.690
what was the general thesis of that?

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:49.777
- So, I shared, it was a
talk on the theory that I--

00:03:49.777 --> 00:03:51.450
- Yeah.
- Continue to espouse

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.730
that I based on an idea
called the golden circle.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.960
Basically, every single
organization on the planet,

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.970
every single one of us knows what we do,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.760
the things we sell, the services we offer,

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.630
some of us know how we
do it, it's the things

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.380
that we think make us
stand out or differentiate

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.740
us from the world outside,
but very, very few

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.750
of us can clearly articulate
why we do what we do.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.930
And if you look at the greatest leaders,

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.000
everybody from Martin
Luther King to Steve Jobs,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.010
those with the capacity to inspire action

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.350
in those around them,
every single one of them,

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:23.460
regardless of their
industry, thinks, acts,

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.010
and communicates starting with why.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:25.843
- Yep.
- Most of us talk

00:04:25.843 --> 00:04:27.240
about what we do, and then we try

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.640
and tell people how we're better.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:29.870
But these guys talk about their vision,

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.703
they talk about their cause,

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.190
they talk about where they're going,

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.500
and what they do simply serves

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.650
as the tangible proof
of what they believe.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.600
And it profoundly changed my life,

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.160
it continues to be the
way in which I organize

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.570
information, make decisions,
set strategy, all of it.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.403
- It's the North Star.

00:04:45.403 --> 00:04:47.300
- It is the North Star.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.210
And I found a language that made it

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.800
really easy to understand, and actually,

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.120
the cool thing is it's actually grounded

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.920
in the biology of decision making.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.440
So it's not like some
highfalutin management theory--

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.120
- Right.
- It's actually grounded

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.770
in how the brain evolved
and makes decisions.

