00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:23.570
- We do a little thing,
which we've been doing

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:26.020
for years and years and
years, called a give-and-take.

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:27.280
Whenever there's any kind of relationship,

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:30.030
whether it's an outside partnership

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.280
or even somebody who joins our team,

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.510
we do something called a give-and-take,

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:36.030
where we want somebody to
be selfish and selfless

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.440
within the relationship.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.500
So, not give-and-get, but give-and-take.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:41.917
So we'll ask them, "What
is it you have to give

00:19:41.917 --> 00:19:44.710
"to us, that you have that
you think that we need?"

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:45.543
And they'll tell us.

00:19:45.543 --> 00:19:46.510
And then we'll say, "Great, what is it

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.780
"that you selfishly want from us?"

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:50.500
And we want them to tell us
what they can get from us

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.400
and no one else.
- I believe in that so much.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.900
- And when those things match,

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.350
you have a balanced relationship.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:56.750
Because, so, for example,
I've had it with people

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.040
who, they'll tell me
what they have to offer,

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.790
and that's awesome,
'cause that's what I want,

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.630
and then they'll say what they wanna take,

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.102
and they go, "Oh, I wanna
work with smart people."

00:20:05.102 --> 00:20:06.737
I'm like, "There are
plenty of smart people.

00:20:06.737 --> 00:20:08.500
"What is it you wanna take from me?"

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.487
They're like, "Oh, I wanna
help build something."

00:20:10.487 --> 00:20:11.957
"Wonderful, do that anywhere.

00:20:11.957 --> 00:20:14.177
"What do you wanna take selfishly from me

00:20:14.177 --> 00:20:15.010
"that you can get nowhere else?"

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:16.085
And if they can't answer the question,

00:20:16.085 --> 00:20:17.870
I won't engage in a relationship,

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:19.970
and the reason is because in time,

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:21.160
the relationship is unbalanced,

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:22.430
they're gonna be giving,
but they're not taking,

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:24.050
and I don't even know how
to give them what they want,

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.503
then they'll complain they're
not making enough money or--

00:20:25.503 --> 00:20:26.500
- Yep, yep.
- Because it's not balanced.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.928
- That's right, and I think--

00:20:27.928 --> 00:20:28.761
- So that's a big part of it.

00:20:28.761 --> 00:20:31.310
- And I think the other thing,
you know, as being out there,

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:35.603
a lot of people play the reverse of that.

00:20:35.603 --> 00:20:36.436
- Yeah.

00:20:36.436 --> 00:20:40.170
