- Be yourself, yeah.

00:27:06.984 --> 00:27:07.817
(India speaks faintly)
- And it's hard

00:27:07.817 --> 00:27:08.690
to be yourself.

00:27:08.690 --> 00:27:09.560
- It takes practice, it's like

00:27:09.560 --> 00:27:10.540
the self-awareness thing, right?

00:27:10.540 --> 00:27:12.050
- Uh-huh, let's do it.

00:27:12.050 --> 00:27:13.730
- [India] From Africa, hold on.

00:27:13.730 --> 00:27:15.048
- Oh, in Africa, I love it.

00:27:15.048 --> 00:27:17.540
- Hi, Gary, my name is Gbenjo Abimbola

00:27:17.540 --> 00:27:19.400
from Nigeria, West Africa.

00:27:19.400 --> 00:27:22.830
It's 2:16 AM in the morning
here, and I'm grinding.

00:27:22.830 --> 00:27:24.198
I hope this gets in.

00:27:24.198 --> 00:27:27.500
My question is short and
simple to you and Simon.

00:27:27.500 --> 00:27:29.410
When do you know you have the chops

00:27:29.410 --> 00:27:31.263
as a young person to start talking,

00:27:32.180 --> 00:27:33.700
when you have the results to back it

00:27:33.700 --> 00:27:36.033
but you're not an all-time great yet?

00:27:36.930 --> 00:27:39.761
Do you start talking, or do you document?

00:27:39.761 --> 00:27:40.823
Thank you.

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:44.470
- I think you start talking.

00:27:44.470 --> 00:27:45.790
The whole thing's a process.

00:27:45.790 --> 00:27:47.210
You start talking immediately.

00:27:47.210 --> 00:27:48.550
I mean, it takes a long time

00:27:48.550 --> 00:27:50.120
to become an overnight success, right?

00:27:50.120 --> 00:27:52.840
And I think for the both of us,

00:27:52.840 --> 00:27:54.650
and everybody we know that we admire

00:27:54.650 --> 00:27:55.890
and who has achieved anything,

00:27:55.890 --> 00:27:56.723
they've been at this a long time--

00:27:56.723 --> 00:27:57.556
- Work!
- And they've been

00:27:57.556 --> 00:27:58.389
talking at it.

00:27:58.389 --> 00:28:00.300
And by the way, they weren't
great at the beginning.

00:28:00.300 --> 00:28:04.410
- Speak for yourself.
- Go watch early interviews

00:28:04.410 --> 00:28:06.140
of Steve Jobs, right?

00:28:06.140 --> 00:28:07.860
Early interviews of
Steve Jobs are fantastic.

00:28:07.860 --> 00:28:09.340
He's terrible!

00:28:09.340 --> 00:28:10.693
And he actually, in one of them,

00:28:10.693 --> 00:28:12.700
says, "I need to go throw up,"

00:28:12.700 --> 00:28:14.610
because he's so nervous
about talking on camera.

00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:15.750
He's terrible!

00:28:15.750 --> 00:28:17.080
And the point is, is he practices

00:28:17.080 --> 00:28:18.120
and he practices and he practices,

00:28:18.120 --> 00:28:20.100
and he gets better, but
he does it out loud.

00:28:20.100 --> 00:28:21.330
And I think the idea of hiding

00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:24.230
until it's perfect, it's a fool's game.

00:28:24.230 --> 00:28:27.110
I think you put yourself
out there, you start,

00:28:27.110 --> 00:28:28.470
you practice, you practice out loud,

00:28:28.470 --> 00:28:31.810
then you get feedback and you can grow.

00:28:31.810 --> 00:28:32.643
- You counterpunch.

00:28:32.643 --> 00:28:34.040
You adjust.
- Yeah, you put it out there.

00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:35.860
- I would say the one thing that you may

00:28:35.860 --> 00:28:38.380
be referring to that
I talk about a lot is,

00:28:38.380 --> 00:28:40.997
it's tough to come out
the gate at 22 and say,

00:28:40.997 --> 00:28:44.220
"This is the definitive
thing, here's my advice."

00:28:44.220 --> 00:28:47.199
I think talking to the
world about your truth--

00:28:47.199 --> 00:28:48.032
- About what you believe.

00:28:48.032 --> 00:28:49.700
- Correct, is the game.
- Yes, is the game.

00:28:49.700 --> 00:28:51.300
- I think what we're
seeing on the Internet

00:28:51.300 --> 00:28:52.360
right now, like, "I'm a"--

00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:55.277
- 22-year-old guru, yeah.
- "I'm a Business coach,

00:28:55.277 --> 00:28:57.157
"and I'm gonna teach you,
and the only business I have

00:28:57.157 --> 00:28:59.437
"is you're gonna pay me
$20K, and I'm gonna teach you

00:28:59.437 --> 00:29:01.120
"how to charge other
people down the ladder

00:29:01.120 --> 00:29:04.460
"$20K to give you guys,"
that's the bad stuff.

00:29:04.460 --> 00:29:07.130
So, your point of view on the world

00:29:07.130 --> 00:29:09.830
and what you believe
and where you come from,

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:11.790
that's gold, your process.

00:29:11.790 --> 00:29:13.980
That's why I talk a lot about documenting

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:14.990
instead of creating.

00:29:14.990 --> 00:29:16.223
It's just your truth.

00:29:17.240 --> 00:29:18.073
But I agree with you.

00:29:18.073 --> 00:29:19.870
I mean, there's no substitute for doing.

00:29:19.870 --> 00:29:23.000
The amount of people that
wait for the perfect thing,

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.630
and then never do anything.
- You know, the most beautiful

00:29:24.630 --> 00:29:26.040
thing when you're young and
you think you have something

00:29:26.040 --> 00:29:28.090
to contribute is to admit that you don't

00:29:28.090 --> 00:29:30.030
know everything, admit
that you're learning.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:30.863
- Yes.
- If you say,

00:29:30.863 --> 00:29:32.227
"I'm a 22-year-old expert, and I can help

00:29:32.227 --> 00:29:35.540
"you do X, Y, and Z," you
actually, it's not true.

00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:36.580
I mean, there's so much more to learn,

00:29:36.580 --> 00:29:37.830
and everybody knows that.

00:29:38.800 --> 00:29:41.400
- Everybody who is the kind
of people that you want.

00:29:41.400 --> 00:29:42.260
- Everybody, yes.
- The people that are

00:29:42.260 --> 00:29:45.360
attracted to that are gonna
do very little for you

00:29:45.360 --> 00:29:46.810
besides some short-term dollars.

00:29:46.810 --> 00:29:48.507
- Agreed, and if you say,
"Look, I'm in this business,

00:29:48.507 --> 00:29:51.047
"I'm fascinated by it, I'm
growing fast, I'm learning fast,

00:29:51.047 --> 00:29:52.240
"I'm still a student of this stuff,

00:29:52.240 --> 00:29:53.820
but I have this service to offer,"

00:29:53.820 --> 00:29:55.940
that humility is unbelievably attractive,

00:29:55.940 --> 00:29:57.610
and people want to be a part of that,

00:29:57.610 --> 00:30:00.040
because they know you're
showing up to learn, not to--

00:30:00.040 --> 00:30:01.257
- Simon, I don't know if you're
paying attention to this,

00:30:01.257 --> 00:30:02.840
but in reverse, what's happening is

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:05.950
people are renting expensive things,

00:30:05.950 --> 00:30:08.593
showing a bullshit lifestyle on Instagram,

00:30:10.740 --> 00:30:13.790
asking their dad to
take $25,000 out in cash

00:30:13.790 --> 00:30:15.120
from the bank, putting it on a bed,

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:16.942
taking a picture, and then
putting it back in the,

00:30:16.942 --> 00:30:21.942
just complete and utter
fraud, and it pisses me off.

00:30:22.470 --> 00:30:23.303
- That's insane.

00:30:23.303 --> 00:30:27.300
- Yeah, and by the way, it's
just a non-winning game.

00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:28.770
- And you only attract
people who want that--

00:30:28.770 --> 00:30:29.655
- The worst.
- And that's not

00:30:29.655 --> 00:30:31.290
even who you are.
- The worst, the worst.

00:30:31.290 --> 00:30:33.300
Anyway, Simon. (claps)
- Probably lying, isn't it?

00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:35.920
- Question of the Day, every guest

00:30:35.920 --> 00:30:37.570
gets to ask the Question of the Day.

00:30:37.570 --> 00:30:38.840
You get to ask them a question,

00:30:38.840 --> 00:30:41.120
you'll get hundreds of data points

00:30:41.120 --> 00:30:41.953
back in return--
- Okay.

00:30:41.953 --> 00:30:45.580
that you can adjust to, both
on Facebook and YouTube.

00:30:45.580 --> 00:30:48.810
So, what would you like
to ask the Vayner Nation?

00:30:48.810 --> 00:30:49.690
What is on your mind?

00:30:49.690 --> 00:30:50.920
What would you like to get a good,

00:30:50.920 --> 00:30:53.820
solid survey in return from?

00:30:53.820 --> 00:30:56.870
- I wanna know, whether
you have your own business

00:30:56.870 --> 00:30:59.810
or work for a bigger
company, I wanna know,

00:30:59.810 --> 00:31:02.580
do you feel loved and supported
by the people around you?

00:31:02.580 --> 00:31:04.380
Do you feel that the
cultures in which you work

00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:06.100
or the culture in which you're building

00:31:06.100 --> 00:31:09.640
are ones of cooperation and of trust?

00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:10.730
Or do you feel that you have to keep

00:31:10.730 --> 00:31:11.610
your guard up the entire time,

00:31:11.610 --> 00:31:12.710
and you can't really trust anybody,

00:31:12.710 --> 00:31:14.140
and you definitely can't trust your boss?

00:31:14.140 --> 00:31:15.330
I wanna know that.

00:31:15.330 --> 00:31:18.040
- And if you are feeling
supported and loved,

00:31:18.040 --> 00:31:19.330
tag that person.

00:31:19.330 --> 00:31:22.870
I think we are just not
deploying enough positivity--

00:31:22.870 --> 00:31:24.220
- Agreed.
- And I think if somebody's

00:31:24.220 --> 00:31:25.930
doing that amazing thing for you,

00:31:25.930 --> 00:31:27.940
they would feel very nice
when this shows up in their

00:31:27.940 --> 00:31:30.450
notifications and realize
they're doing that for you.

00:31:30.450 --> 00:31:31.469
- Yeah, thanks very much,

00:31:31.469 --> 00:31:32.406
yeah, wonderful.
- Yeah, love you, pal.

00:31:32.406 --> 00:31:33.239
(hands slap)

00:31:33.239 --> 00:31:34.072
- Thanks a lot.
- Real good.

00:31:34.072 --> 00:31:37.159
You keep asking questions,
we'll keep answering them.

